# lawsynth-scheduler reads no environment variables. Its configuration is passed
# as explicit CLI arguments (`serve <addr> [root]`), and its bounds are the
# compiled-in SchedulerConfig/StoreConfig defaults documented under config/.
#
# Keep this file free of secrets. The control plane has no principals or tokens;
# authentication and TLS belong to a separately deployed front door, not to this
# process. If a future deployment wrapper needs machine-specific paths, place
# them in an untracked .env and document the key here first.
#
# SCHEDULER_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8082                     # example only; not read by the binary
# SCHEDULER_STORE_ROOT=/var/lib/lawsynth/scheduler # example only; not read by the binary
